<p>This page allows you to remove your account.</p>
<p>There are two types of removal: <i>soft</i> and <i>hard</i>.</p>
<p><i>Soft</i> removal will remove all groups from your account and replace them with <i>Deleted</i> group. If you change your mind and want to return to the website, you can <a href="/about/contacts">contact</a> administration to have your account restored.</p>
<p><i>Hard</i> removal will replace your internal user ID with one for <a href="/talks/users/3"><i>Deleted user</i></a> for all content created, including files uploaded, and then remove your user <b>entirely</b>, that is <b>without the ability to restore</b> at a later day.</p>
<p>If such unlinking of your account from respective content is not enough, please, create a post in <a href="/talks/sections/5">Support</a>, so that the administration can check and ensure that some potentially useful information is not lost.</p>
<form id="user_removal" class="middle" method="post">
    <span class="float_label">
        <input id="hard_removal" type="checkbox">
        <label for="hard_removal">
            <span class="checkbox_checked_icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="checkbox_checked">I want it hard</span>
            <span class="checkbox_not_checked_icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="checkbox_not_checked">I want it hard</span>
        </label>
    </span>
    <br>
    <button type="submit" name="submit" id="remove_user" value="Remove me" data-alt-attribute="Removing user...">
        <span class="warning">Remove me</span>
    </button>
</form>
